.TH PODFEED 1 "2026-08-08" "podfeed 0.3.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
podfeed \- generate podcast RSS feeds from yt-dlp metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B podfeed generate
.BI \-d " PATH"
.BI \-\-base-url " URL"
.br
.B podfeed generate-completion
.I SHELL
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B podfeed
creates podcast RSS feeds from media files and
.B .info.json
metadata files created by
.BR yt-dlp (1).
Each channel directory gets an adjacent XML feed.
.B podfeed
creates square 1400×1400 channel and episode artwork when needed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B generate
Generate feeds for all channel directories below the data directory.
.TP
.B generate-completion
Write a shell completion script to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS generate
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-data-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Root directory containing channel directories created by yt-dlp.
May also be supplied with the
.B DATADIR
environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-\-base-url " URL"
Public URL corresponding to the data directory. It is used for media and
artwork URLs in generated feeds.
May also be supplied with the
.B BASEURL
environment variable.
.SS generate-completion
.TP
.I SHELL
Target shell. One of
.BR bash ,
.BR elvish ,
.BR fish ,
.BR powershell ,
or
.BR zsh .
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate feeds for a yt-dlp data directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
podfeed generate \
  --data-dir ./data \
  --base-url https://podcasts.example.com
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate a Bash completion script:
.PP
.RS
.nf
podfeed generate-completion bash > podfeed.bash
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DATADIR
Default value for
.BR \-\-data-dir .
.TP
.B BASEURL
Default value for
.BR \-\-base-url .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Feeds or a completion script were generated successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
An input, image-processing, or output error occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt-dlp (1)
.SH AUTHORS
graelo <https://github.com/graelo/podfeed>
